PART 6 -- correction to monad-S1's 'the bounded window IS the covering case':
          a PRIMITIVE COVERING set with V/spread >> 2.8 exists at every scale
====================================================================================================
S = [302, 309, 316, 325, 330, 336, 344, 351, 360, 372, 374, 390, 392]
covering: True   primitive: True   13 distinct: True
Vmax = 392, spread = 90, V/spread = 4.4  (>> 2.8: OUTSIDE the window)
M = 151/347 = 0.4352 >= 1/14: True   (drift-embed regime, as expected easy)
=> covering does NOT force V/spread ~ 1; the correct statement is: the HARD covering
   clusters (small caps / forced small speeds) are in the window.  At every scale there
   are also easy covering clusters outside it.

Done.
